.TH t69 1 "July 2026" "6ix9ine v1.0.0" "t69 Dashboard Manual"
.SH NAME
t69 \- Terminal User Interface (TUI) dashboard for 6ix9ine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B t69
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B t69
is the interactive terminal dashboard for the
.BR 6ix9ine (1)
sleep-blocking daemon. It provides a real-time visualization of current sleep assertions, active agent sessions, timed holds, CPU temperature, lid state, and auxiliary developer dependencies (e.g., Docker, Ollama).
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B q
Quit the dashboard.
.TP
.B k
Kill the selected active session.
.TP
.B x
Purge/kill all active sleep-blocking sessions.
.TP
.B a
Ignore (quietly filter out) a module from the auxiliary dashboard.
.TP
.B r
Restore an ignored auxiliary module.
.TP
.B Up / Down / Mouse Wheel
Select and navigate between active sessions in the registry.
.TP
.B Enter
Inspect details of the selected session (e.g., agent, PID, UUID, start time, reason).
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the live dashboard:
.IP
.B t69
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 6ix9ine (1)
